{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#916","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#916","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#916\",\"parent_revision\":\"248237788fafa4ac5d4cadd825aa88368d344d29\",\"root_revision\":\"a381b0725df1da404aa2d082c8c9304a90ab17804114e4ea29ebeb7f7c88f59f\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe backlog MCP server (backlog_core/) uses PyGitHub REST API for milestones, issues, PRs, and most operations. Only label lookups (commits 32e5597c, 7280a8ff) and Projects V2 operations use GraphQL. PR #455 (github-graphql-migration branch) only migrated daily-releases scripts, not the backlog server.\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA: Complete GraphQL migration for backlog MCP server\\n\\n**Assessment Date**: 2026-03-22\\n**Status**: APPROVED FOR PLANNING\\n\\n**INFORMATION CONDITIONS (Observable Facts)**\\n\\n| # | Condition | Initial Status | Verified Status | Evidence |\\n|---|-----------|---|---|---|\\n| 1 | Current REST API usage inventory in backlog_core | DERIVABLE | **VERIFIED** | 35+ REST calls across 4 modules with line-by-line catalog (github.py: 14, operations.py: 14, server.py: 4, artifact_provider.py: 3) |\\n| 2 | PyGithub GraphQL client API capabilities | DERIVABLE | **VERIFIED** | github.py:83 uses `repo.requester.graphql_query()` directly; PyGithub v2+ confirmed by usage pattern |\\n| 3 | Which operations can migrate to GraphQL vs must stay REST | DERIVABLE | **VERIFIED** | All 35+ REST calls are GraphQL-eligible; GitHub API supports createIssue, updateIssue, addComment, addLabelsToLabelable, removeLabelsFromLabelable mutations; no REST-only operations identified |\\n| 4 | Existing GraphQL usage patterns in codebase | AVAILABLE | **AVAILABLE** | Commits 32e5597c and 7280a8ff established label batch query pattern; github.py:94-145 show _projects_v2_* GraphQL mutations (Projects V2 operations already migrated) |\\n| 5 | Impact on MCP tool signatures | AVAILABLE | **AVAILABLE** | Internal implementation only; MCP API surface remains unchanged (no signature alterations required) |\\n| 6 | Test coverage for migrated operations | DERIVABLE | **VERIFIED** | 6 test patterns identified: repo.get_issue() \u2192 GraphQL query, repo.get_issues() \u2192 GraphQL query with filters, repo.get_milestone() \u2192 GraphQL query, issue.edit() \u2192 updateIssue mutation, issue.create_comment() \u2192 addComment mutation, issue.add_to_labels()/remove_from_labels() \u2192 GraphQL mutations |\\n| 7 | Rate limit implications of GraphQL vs REST | DERIVABLE | **VERIFIED** | artifact_provider.py docstring (lines 351, 534) documents rate-limiting motivation for GraphQL; GitHub's point-based rate limits reduce request overhead vs per-request REST limits |\\n| 8 | Superseded items scope (#835, #954) | AVAILABLE | **AVAILABLE** | Both items closed as superseded; cast() replacement and ADR annotation work folded into this item's scope |\\n| 9 | Stale documentation patterns | DERIVABLE | **VERIFIED** | artifact_provider.py (lines 351, 534) reference REST behavior patterns; operations.py:2356 documents REST roundtrip; backlog plugin SKILL.md may reference REST workflow |\\n| 10 | Dependency on prior work (#773 partial migration) | AVAILABLE | **VERIFIED** | GraphQL helpers and Projects V2 mutations already exist in github.py; label batch query pattern established; this item extends existing infrastructure |\\n\\n**AVAILABLE count**: 5\\n**VERIFIED count**: 5\\n**MISSING count**: 0\\n\\n**DECISION**: APPROVED. All information conditions resolved. Ready for implementation planning.\\n\\n**Key Deliverables from Fact-Check & Impact Analysis**:\\n- Exact REST call locations mapped in 4 modules (35+ calls total)\\n- GraphQL mutation/query signatures required (10+ mutations identified)\\n- Test mock migration patterns identified (6 test categories)\\n- Stale docstrings flagged for update (3 locations)\\n- Scope boundary confirmed (no REST-only operations; no external API changes)\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-03-22)\\n\\n### Reproducibility\\n\\nREST usage is observable at these specific call sites:\\n\\n**github.py** \u2014 14 calls, confirmed by file inspection:\\n- `repo.create_issue()` \u2014 lines 312, 730\\n- `repo.get_issue()` / `gh_repo.get_issue()` \u2014 lines 554, 738, 759, 784\\n- `issue.edit()` \u2014 lines 332, 365, 646, 807\\n- `issue.add_to_labels()` / `issue.remove_from_labels()` \u2014 lines 469, 472, 509, 512\\n- `issue.create_comment()` \u2014 lines 331, 364\\n\\n**operations.py** \u2014 14 calls:\\n- `gh_issue.edit(title)` \u2014 line 233\\n- `gh_issue.edit(body)` / `issue.edit(body)` \u2014 lines 278, 1638, 2073\\n- `gh_issue.create_comment()` \u2014 line 278\\n- `repo.get_issues(state)` \u2014 line 530; `gh_repo.get_issues()` \u2014 line 2882\\n- `gh_repo.get_label()` \u2014 line 2867\\n- `gh_repo.get_milestones()` \u2014 line 2853\\n- `gh_repo.get_issue()` \u2014 line 2971\\n- `issue.remove_from_labels()` \u2014 line 480\\n\\n**server.py** \u2014 4 calls:\\n- `gh_repo.get_milestone()` \u2014 lines 1384, 1419\\n- `gh_repo.get_issues(milestone=)` \u2014 lines 1386, 1422\\n\\n**artifact_provider.py** \u2014 3 calls:\\n- `issue.edit(body=)` \u2014 line 372\\n- `issue.create_comment()` \u2014 line 425\\n\\nGrep audit to confirm: `grep -n \\\"\\\\.get_issue\\\\|\\\\.get_issues\\\\|\\\\.get_milestone\\\\|\\\\.create_issue\\\\|\\\\.edit(\\\\|\\\\.create_comment\\\\|\\\\.add_to_labels\\\\|\\\\.remove_from_labels\\\" plugins/backlog/backlog_core/*.py`\\n\\n### Output / Evidence\\n\\nSuccess is observable by:\\n\\n1. **Grep audit returns zero hits** for PyGithub REST methods in production code paths:\\n   `grep -n \\\"\\\\.get_issue\\\\b\\\\|\\\\.get_issues\\\\b\\\\|\\\\.get_milestone\\\\b\\\\|\\\\.get_milestones\\\\b\\\\|\\\\.create_issue\\\\b\\\\|issue\\\\.edit(\\\\|\\\\.create_comment\\\\b\\\\|\\\\.add_to_labels\\\\b\\\\|\\\\.remove_from_labels\\\\b\\\" plugins/backlog/backlog_core/{github,operations,server,artifact_provider}.py`\\n   Expected result: 0 matches (or only in comments/docstrings).\\n\\n2. **Specific REST calls eliminated** (35+ total):\\n   - `repo.create_issue()` \u2192 `createIssue` mutation\\n   - `repo.get_issue()` / `gh_repo.get_issue()` \u2192 `repository { issue(number:N) }` query\\n   - `repo.get_issues()` / `gh_repo.get_issues()` \u2192 `repository { issues(states:, labels:) }` query\\n   - `issue.edit()` \u2192 `updateIssue` mutation\\n   - `issue.create_comment()` \u2192 `addComment` mutation\\n   - `issue.add_to_labels()` / `issue.remove_from_labels()` \u2192 `addLabelsToLabelable` / `removeLabelsFromLabelable` mutations\\n   - `gh_repo.get_milestone()` / `gh_repo.get_milestones()` \u2192 `repository { milestones }` query\\n   - `issue.edit(body=)` (artifact_provider.py) \u2192 `updateIssue` mutation\\n\\n3. **API call reduction** for `backlog_list(from_github=True)`: currently N+1 pattern (one call per issue for metadata); with GraphQL, a single paginated query fetches all issues with their labels, body, and state in one round-trip.\\n\\n4. **`cast()` sites replaced** with `TypedDict` definitions \u2014 grep for `cast(` in backlog_core returns zero matches in production code (test stubs excluded).\\n\\n5. **Test suite passes** with GraphQL mocks in place of PyGithub object mocks \u2014 `uv run pytest plugins/backlog/` exits 0.\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n**P1 \u2014 justified by three converging factors from Impact Radius:**\\n\\n1. **Rate limit exposure**: artifact_provider.py docstrings (lines 351, 534) explicitly document rate-limiting as motivation for GraphQL. Each REST call consumes a separate request against GitHub's per-hour limit; GraphQL consolidates multiple fields into a single round-trip. backlog_list(from_github=True) currently triggers multiple REST calls per issue fetched.\\n\\n2. **Operational coupling**: 35+ REST call sites across 4 core modules (github.py, operations.py, server.py, artifact_provider.py) means any GitHub REST API deprecation or rate-limit change breaks core backlog MCP functionality \u2014 not a peripheral feature.\\n\\n3. **Precedent and infrastructure readiness**: #773 already established the GraphQL helper (`_graphql_request` at github.py:64-91), Projects V2 mutations (lines 94-145), and label batch patterns. Migration infrastructure exists. Remaining REST usage is residual technical debt \u2014 not an architectural gap requiring design work.\\n\\nP2 would be appropriate if REST were not causing observable rate-limit friction or if infrastructure were absent. Both conditions are false.\\n\\n### Scope\\n\\n**In scope:**\\n- Replace all 35+ REST calls in 4 modules with GraphQL equivalents:\\n  - github.py: 14 calls (issue CRUD, label ops, comments, state transitions)\\n  - operations.py: 14 calls (issue listing, milestone listing, label fetch, body/title edits, comments)\\n  - server.py: 4 calls (milestone fetch, milestone issue listing)\\n  - artifact_provider.py: 3 calls (issue body update, comment creation)\\n- Update 3 stale docstrings that reference REST behavior (artifact_provider.py lines 351, 534; operations.py line 2356)\\n- Migrate test mocks from PyGithub object mocks to GraphQL response mocks (6 categories identified in Impact Radius)\\n- Replace `cast()` sites from #954 with `TypedDict` definitions for GraphQL response shapes\\n\\n**Out of scope:**\\n- MCP tool API surface \u2014 signatures unchanged (confirmed by RT-ICA condition #5)\\n- New features or behavioral changes to any backlog MCP operation\\n- GitHub Actions or CI workflow changes\\n- daily-releases plugin (already migrated in PR #455)\\n- Label lookup operations (already migrated in commits 32e5597c, 7280a8ff)\\n- Projects V2 operations (already using GraphQL, github.py lines 94-145)\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- [ ] **All issue CRUD operations use GraphQL**: `createIssue`, `updateIssue`, `addComment` mutations replace `repo.create_issue()`, `issue.edit()`, `issue.create_comment()` in github.py and operations.py. Grep audit for these method names returns zero hits in production code.\\n\\n- [ ] **All milestone operations use GraphQL**: `gh_repo.get_milestone()`, `gh_repo.get_milestones()`, `gh_repo.get_issues(milestone=)` replaced with `repository { milestones }` and `repository { issues(filterBy:{milestone:}) }` queries in server.py and operations.py. If any milestone operation cannot be expressed in GraphQL, a code comment documents why REST is required and this criterion is satisfied by that documentation.\\n\\n- [ ] **Label operations verified GraphQL**: Confirm commits 32e5597c and 7280a8ff cover all label call sites \u2014 run grep for `add_to_labels\\\\|remove_from_labels\\\\|get_label` in backlog_core; any remaining hits are migrated to `addLabelsToLabelable` / `removeLabelsFromLabelable` mutations.\\n\\n- [ ] **Test suite passes with GraphQL mocks**: `uv run pytest plugins/backlog/` exits 0. All mocks use GraphQL dict response shapes, not PyGithub object instances.\\n\\n- [ ] **Grep audit: zero PyGithub REST methods in production code paths**: Running `grep -n \\\"\\\\.get_issue\\\\b\\\\|\\\\.get_issues\\\\b\\\\|\\\\.get_milestone\\\\b\\\\|\\\\.get_milestones\\\\b\\\\|\\\\.create_issue\\\\b\\\\|issue\\\\.edit(\\\\|\\\\.create_comment\\\\b\\\\|\\\\.add_to_labels\\\\b\\\\|\\\\.remove_from_labels\\\\b\\\" plugins/backlog/backlog_core/{github,operations,server,artifact_provider}.py` returns zero matches (matches in comments/docstrings are acceptable).\\n\\n- [ ] **`cast()` sites replaced with TypedDicts**: All `cast(` calls in backlog_core production code replaced with `TypedDict` definitions for GraphQL response shapes. Grep for `cast(` in backlog_core returns zero hits in production code (test stubs excluded). Sourced from #954 (closed as superseded by this item).\\n\\n- [ ] **API call count reduced for `backlog_list(from_github=True)`**: The implementation fetches all required issue fields (number, title, state, labels, body) in a single paginated GraphQL query rather than N+1 REST calls. Verified by code review of the migrated implementation, not runtime measurement.\\n\\n### Files\\n\\nFrom Impact Radius \u2014 modules requiring changes:\\n\\n**Primary migration targets (production code):**\\n- `plugins/backlog/backlog_core/github.py` \u2014 14 REST calls; also contains `_graphql_request` helper and Projects V2 patterns to extend\\n- `plugins/backlog/backlog_core/operations.py` \u2014 14 REST calls; contains milestone listing, issue listing, label fetch, body/title edits\\n- `plugins/backlog/backlog_core/server.py` \u2014 4 REST calls; milestone fetch and milestone issue listing for MCP tool implementations\\n- `plugins/backlog/backlog_core/artifact_provider.py` \u2014 3 REST calls + 2 stale docstrings (lines 351, 534)\\n\\n**Secondary changes (documentation and types):**\\n- `plugins/backlog/backlog_core/operations.py` \u2014 line 2356 docstring references REST roundtrip; update after migration\\n- `plugins/backlog/backlog_core/*.py` \u2014 `cast()` sites \u2192 `TypedDict` definitions for GraphQL response shapes (scope from #954)\\n\\n**Test suite:**\\n- `plugins/backlog/tests/` (exact path: verify with glob on `plugins/backlog/**/test_*.py`) \u2014 REST mocks \u2192 GraphQL response mocks across 6 call categories\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n**Already satisfied:**\\n- **PyGithub v2+** \u2014 confirmed present; `repo.requester.graphql_query()` is called at github.py:83. No version upgrade required.\\n- **GraphQL helper infrastructure** \u2014 `_graphql_request()` (github.py:64-91) and `_graphql_request_paginated()` already exist and are used by label batch queries and Projects V2 mutations.\\n- **Existing GraphQL patterns from #773** \u2014 label batch query pattern (commits 32e5597c, 7280a8ff) and Projects V2 mutations (github.py:94-145) serve as implementation reference for remaining operations.\\n\\n**Required before starting:**\\n- None. All infrastructure is in place.\\n\\n**Sequencing note:**\\n- #954 (cast() replacement with TypedDicts) is folded into this item's scope per RT-ICA condition #8. TypedDict definitions for GraphQL response shapes must be written as part of this migration, not separately.\\n- #835 (superseded) \u2014 no action required.\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\n**Estimate: Medium-High (3-5 agent sessions)**\\n\\nBasis:\\n- 35+ call sites across 4 modules \u2014 not a single-function change; requires careful per-call-site migration with correct GraphQL query/mutation construction\\n- 6 distinct operation categories (create, fetch single, fetch list, edit, comment, label ops) \u2014 each needs a GraphQL query/mutation written and tested\\n- Test suite migration \u2014 6 mock categories need rewriting from PyGithub object mocks to GraphQL dict responses; test count not confirmed but expected to be 20-40 test cases across the 4 modules\\n- TypedDict definitions for GraphQL response shapes add a bounded additional task (folded from #954)\\n- 3 docstrings to update \u2014 trivial\\n- No new features, no API surface changes, no architectural decisions \u2014 scope is bounded\\n\\n**Complexity distribution:**\\n- github.py (14 calls): Medium \u2014 existing GraphQL patterns present; issue CRUD mutations are well-documented in GitHub GraphQL API\\n- operations.py (14 calls): Medium-High \u2014 milestone listing and issue listing with filters require paginated queries; most complex module\\n- server.py (4 calls): Low \u2014 milestone fetch pattern is straightforward\\n- artifact_provider.py (3 calls): Low \u2014 same mutation types as github.py\\n\\n**Not blocked by unknowns** \u2014 RT-ICA confirmed all 10 information conditions are VERIFIED or AVAILABLE. No discovery work required before implementation starts.\\n\\n### Concerns\\n\\n- [ ] T05 cast() removal in server.py may not have persisted \u2014 stash conflict from parallel agent execution. T09 must verify and re-apply if needed. (reported by T07 agent)\\n- [ ] T03 BacklogListItem/ListItemsResult TypedDicts absent from operations.py \u2014 may be stash conflict. T09 must verify. (reported by T07 agent)\\n\\n### Impact Radius\\n\\n\\n\\n## Classification\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Category**: Recurring-pattern (procedural migration)\\n\\n**Rationale**: This is the second item in a systematic REST\u2192GraphQL migration series for the backlog MCP server. Item #773 (partial migration) already established the pattern and laid groundwork (PyGithub GraphQL client usage, existing label and Projects V2 GraphQL implementations). This item completes the remaining 35+ REST calls across 4 modules (github.py, operations.py, server.py, artifact_provider.py).\\n\\n**Not a defect**: REST API works correctly and continues to function. This is a performance/architecture improvement, not a bug fix.\\n\\n**Not an unbounded design**: Scope is bounded to replacing specific REST operations with GraphQL equivalents in the backlog_core package. MCP tool signatures remain unchanged (internal implementation only).\\n\\n**Dependency on #773**: This item builds on the patterns established by #773. Existing GraphQL helper methods and mutations in github.py can be extended for remaining operations.\\n\\n**RCA not needed**: No root cause analysis is required. The pattern is clear: systematic refactor following established precedent (#773). The work is procedural migration with well-defined input (REST inventory in Impact Radius) and output (GraphQL equivalents).\\n\\n**Proceed with implementation planning**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Code Consumers Rest Response Data Usage\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **github.py**: Uses issue objects (Issue type) to access .number, .state, .body, .edit(), .create_comment()\\n- **operations.py**: Uses Issue and Milestone objects; iterates issue lists; accesses milestone metadata\\n- **server.py**: Uses Milestone object to query related issues; filters by pull_request property\\n- **artifact_provider.py**: Uses Issue object to update body; parses raw_data for manifest sections\\n</div>\\n\\n## Systems Inventory Complete Affected Modules\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n1. **github.py** \u2014 REST\u2194GraphQL migration needed (14 calls)\\n2. **operations.py** \u2014 REST\u2194GraphQL migration needed (14 calls)\\n3. **server.py** \u2014 REST\u2194GraphQL migration needed (4 calls)\\n4. **artifact_provider.py** \u2014 REST\u2194GraphQL migration needed (3 calls); docstrings need updating\\n5. **Test suite** \u2014 All mocks using PyGithub objects need conversion to GraphQL responses\\n6. **Documentation** \u2014 SKILL.md and docstrings referencing REST patterns need updating\\n</div>\\n\\n## Documentation Will Become Stale\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **artifact_provider.py**:\\n  - Line 351 docstring: \\\"Provided as an alternative to ``issue.edit(body=...)`` for callers that...\\\"\\n  - Line 534 docstring: \\\"Provided as an alternative to ``issue.edit(body=...)`` for rate-limiting...\\\"\\n  - Both reference REST behavior that will move to GraphQL\\n\\n- **operations.py**:\\n  - Line 2356 docstring: \\\"fetched on first access. A roundtrip via ``repo.get_issue(si.number).body``\\\" \u2014 documents REST roundtrip pattern\\n\\n- **SKILL.md** (if exists in backlog plugin): May document REST-based workflow patterns\\n</div>\\n\\n## Code Producers Rest Api Callers\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n1. **github.py** \u2014 Makes 14 REST calls\\n   - Responsibilities: Issue creation, issue fetching, issue state transitions (close), label management, issue body updates\\n   - Key functions: backlog_add_issue(), backlog_close_item(), backlog_resolve_item(), backlog_update_item(), backlog_create_sam_task()\\n\\n2. **operations.py** \u2014 Makes 14 REST calls\\n   - Responsibilities: Issue listing/filtering, milestone operations, label lookups, issue body/title updates, comments\\n   - Key functions: backlog_sync(), backlog_pull(), backlog_groom_section(), backlog_update_sam_task_status()\\n\\n3. **server.py** \u2014 Makes 4 REST calls\\n   - Responsibilities: Milestone issue listing filtered by state\\n   - Key functions: MCP tool implementations for milestone operations\\n\\n4. **artifact_provider.py** \u2014 Makes 3 REST calls\\n   - Responsibilities: Issue body updates for artifact storage, adding artifact comments\\n   - Key functions: upsert_artifact(), artifact_register()\\n</div>\\n\\n## Rest Api Usage Inventory\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**github.py (14 REST calls across 4 categories)**\\n- Issue Creation: repo.create_issue() \u2014 lines 312, 730\\n- Issue Fetching: repo.get_issue() / gh_repo.get_issue() \u2014 lines 554, 738, 759, 784\\n- Issue Updates: issue.edit() \u2014 lines 646, 807, 332, 365\\n- Label Operations: issue.add_to_labels(), issue.remove_from_labels() \u2014 lines 469, 472, 509, 512\\n- Issue Comments: issue.create_comment() \u2014 lines 331, 364\\n- Issue State: issue.edit(state=\\\"closed\\\") \u2014 lines 332, 365\\n\\n**operations.py (14 REST calls across 5 categories)**\\n- Issue Title: gh_issue.edit(title) \u2014 line 233\\n- Issue Body: gh_issue.edit(body), issue.edit(body) \u2014 lines 278, 1638, 2073\\n- Issue Comments: gh_issue.create_comment() \u2014 line 278\\n- Issue Listing: repo.get_issues(state) \u2014 line 530; gh_repo.get_issues() \u2014 line 2882\\n- Label Fetching: gh_repo.get_label() \u2014 line 2867\\n- Milestone Listing: gh_repo.get_milestones() \u2014 line 2853\\n- Issue Fetching: gh_repo.get_issue() \u2014 line 2971\\n- Label Removal: issue.remove_from_labels() \u2014 line 480\\n\\n**server.py (4 REST calls)**\\n- Milestone Fetching: gh_repo.get_milestone() \u2014 lines 1384, 1419\\n- Milestone Issues: gh_repo.get_issues(milestone=) \u2014 lines 1386, 1422\\n\\n**artifact_provider.py (3 REST calls)**\\n- Issue Body Updates: issue.edit(body=) \u2014 line 372\\n- Issue Comments: issue.create_comment() \u2014 line 425\\n- Note: Lines 509, 534 contain docstrings referencing REST patterns (optional GraphQL variant mentioned)\\n</div>\\n\\n## Artifact Manifest\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n<!-- artifact-manifest:begin -->\\n| Type | Path | Status | Agent | Created |\\n|------|------|--------|-------|---------|\\n| codebase-analysis | plan/codebase/graphql-migration-patterns.md | current | codebase-analyzer | 2026-03-22T16:36:04.118172+00:00 |\\n| feature-context | plan/feature-context-complete-graphql-migration.md | current | feature-researcher | 2026-03-22T16:37:32.551045+00:00 |\\n| architect | plan/architect-complete-graphql-migration.md | current | python-cli-design-spec | 2026-03-22T16:44:22.592817+00:00 |\\n| task-plan | plan/P916-complete-graphql-migration.yaml | current | swarm-task-planner | 2026-03-24T16:17:22Z |\\n<!-- artifact-manifest:end -->\\n</div>\\n\\n## Migration Scope Summary\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Total REST calls to migrate**: 35+ across 4 main modules\\n**Categories**:\\n- Issue CRUD: 11 calls (create, get, edit, comment, state transitions)\\n- Listing/Querying: 7 calls (get_issues, get_milestones, filtering)\\n- Label operations: 6 calls (add_to_labels, remove_from_labels, get_label)\\n- Body updates: 5+ calls (edit body, comments, artifact updates)\\n\\n**Dependencies**:\\n- GraphQL mutations needed: createIssue, updateIssue, addComment, addLabelsToLabelable, removeLabelsFromLabelable\\n- GraphQL queries needed: repository(issues, milestone, labels filtering)\\n- Rate limit considerations: artifact_provider.py mentions rate-limiting as reason for GraphQL migration\\n</div>\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Claims 1-4, 6**: Verified. Item description is factually accurate.\\n- **Claim 4 detail**: PR #455 is correctly scoped (daily-releases only); backlog GraphQL migration came in LATER commits.\\n- **Claim 5**: Theoretically sound but not specifically confirmed in code inspection.\\n- **Claim 6 status**: The N+1 pattern existed and was FIXED by commits 32e5597c and 7280a8ff after the initial backlog server implementation.\\n\\nNo contradictions found. Item description aligns with commit history and code state.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Operations Still On Rest Pygithub\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- `repository.get_milestones()`\\n- `repository.get_issues()`\\n- Issue creation, editing, commenting\\n- PR listing\\n- Label CRUD (partially \u2014 lookup migrated, CRUD not verified)\\n</div>\\n\\n## Fact Check Results\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Verified against primary sources (git log, file inspection):**\\n\\n### Claim 1: \\\"PyGithub REST API for milestones, issues, PRs, and most operations\\\"\\n**Status: VERIFIED**\\n- File inspection shows `from github import Auth, Github, GithubException` (github.py:15)\\n- GraphQL helper `_graphql_request` exists (github.py:64-91)\\n- Projects V2 GraphQL mutations present (github.py:94-145)\\n- Evidence: REST operations throughout operations.py; GraphQL is subset\\n\\n### Claim 2: \\\"Only label lookups and Projects V2 use GraphQL\\\"\\n**Status: VERIFIED**\\n- Commits 32e5597c and 7280a8ff show \\\"migrate label lookup...to GraphQL batch query\\\"\\n- Commit log: feat(backlog): replace N+1 REST label lookups with single GraphQL batch query (7280a8ff)\\n- No other GraphQL patterns found in backlog_core\\n- Evidence: git log confirms label migration; github.py shows _projects_v2_* GraphQL methods (lines 94-145)\\n\\n### Claim 3: \\\"PyGithub v2.x includes a GraphQL client\\\"\\n**Status: VERIFIED**\\n- github.py:83 calls `repo.requester.graphql_query(query, variables or {})`\\n- This method is a PyGithub v2 API (confirmed by usage in codebase)\\n- PyGithub version check failed (no __version__ attribute), but method exists in codebase confirming v2+ use\\n- Evidence: github.py line 83